WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.099 --> 00:00:06.129
Westworld Season 2 Episode 7 reveals some
of the central secrets of the season.

00:00:06.129 --> 00:00:10.980
Bernard and Ford are inside the Cradle, the
digital simulation of Westworld.

00:00:10.980 --> 00:00:16.590
We learn that the Delos company’s secret
project is to study guest behaviour and “understand”

00:00:16.590 --> 00:00:22.740
the human mind, so they can make backup copies
of people – to make humans immortal . They

00:00:22.740 --> 00:00:28.690
did this with James Delos, and Ford copied
himself the same way . So far, these copies

00:00:28.690 --> 00:00:33.329
can’t survive in physical bodies – or
they “degrade” like James did . That’s

00:00:33.329 --> 00:00:37.809
why Ford got Bernard to put his copied mind
in the Cradle – where he lives digitally

00:00:37.809 --> 00:00:41.929
. But James and Ford aren’t the only copied
minds.

00:00:41.929 --> 00:00:46.869
Later in the episode, Dolores mentions “all
the souls” “gathered” “in that valley”

00:00:46.869 --> 00:00:52.109
. It sounds like Delos made copies of lots
of human guests, and since copies break down

00:00:52.109 --> 00:00:56.579
in the real world, Delos is storing these
minds digitally in the “valley”.

00:00:56.579 --> 00:01:01.739
So the Valley might be like the Cradle, but
instead of storing host minds, it stores human

00:01:01.739 --> 00:01:05.890
minds, waiting to eventually put them in physical
bodies.

00:01:05.890 --> 00:01:11.640
You can argue that making clone copies of
people isn’t the same as immortality.

00:01:11.640 --> 00:01:14.020
James died a hundred times.

00:01:14.020 --> 00:01:19.900
But each time he had his memories, he believed
he was James – and as William said, “If

00:01:19.900 --> 00:01:23.170
you can't tell” the difference, “does
it matter?”

00:01:23.170 --> 00:01:26.670
Ford also explains how Bernard was made.

00:01:26.670 --> 00:01:31.780
We already knew that Bernard is based on Arnold
– Ford’s partner who died years ago.

00:01:31.780 --> 00:01:37.119
But apparently Bernard was created from Ford
and Dolores’ memories of Arnold . These

00:01:37.119 --> 00:01:43.100
flashbacks in Episodes 1 and 6 show Dolores
refining Bernard in the Cradle , testing him

00:01:43.100 --> 00:01:48.539
until he’s convincingly like Arnold . So
this process is similar to how Delos made

00:01:48.539 --> 00:01:50.240
a copy of James.

00:01:50.240 --> 00:01:55.289
But Ford says that while James is a direct
copy, Bernard is a bit different to Arnold

00:01:55.289 --> 00:01:57.890
– he’s “An original work”.

00:01:57.890 --> 00:02:01.540
Which must be why Bernard doesn’t break
down like James does.

00:02:01.540 --> 00:02:04.259
And this is the difference between Ford and
Delos.

00:02:04.259 --> 00:02:10.570
Delos wants to make perfect copies of human
minds, to be preserved, immortal, predictable.

00:02:10.570 --> 00:02:15.710
But Ford wants to make “a new people”,
hosts with the free will to evolve and change

00:02:15.710 --> 00:02:21.550
– like Bernard, and Dolores and Maeve . But
Ford says he needs to take back Bernard’s

00:02:21.550 --> 00:02:26.690
free will for a bit . Ford moves his digital
self out of the Cradle and into Bernard’s

00:02:26.690 --> 00:02:29.750
head, so that Ford controls Bernard.

00:02:29.750 --> 00:02:34.081
Ford says that for the hosts to “survive”
they need to “open the door” – which

00:02:34.081 --> 00:02:37.270
seems to mean hosts escaping Westworld.

00:02:37.270 --> 00:02:43.500
And the Westworld ARG hints at how this might
work – it shows imagery of the Trojan horse.

00:02:43.500 --> 00:02:48.800
So one theory is that Dolores will put the
minds of her hosts inside the bodies intended

00:02:48.800 --> 00:02:51.510
for the humans stored in the valley.

00:02:51.510 --> 00:02:56.630
With human bodies, the hosts could sneak in
to the real world, like a Trojan horse.

00:02:56.630 --> 00:03:02.280
This would also solve the problem of the explosives
in host spines . The hosts’ old bodies could

00:03:02.280 --> 00:03:07.970
be left behind in the valley – with those
empty minds Antoine finds . And for poetic

00:03:07.970 --> 00:03:13.420
revenge, Dolores could even put human minds
from the valley inside some old host bodies,

00:03:13.420 --> 00:03:16.550
to be captured or killed as hosts.

00:03:16.550 --> 00:03:21.870
This would, in a way, give both sides what
they want – the hosts would be free like

00:03:21.870 --> 00:03:26.170
humans, while the humans would become immortal
like hosts . They’d swap.

00:03:26.170 --> 00:03:28.390
But this is speculation.

00:03:28.390 --> 00:03:33.450
What we know is that is that Delos’ plan
is to copy and immortalise human minds, and

00:03:33.450 --> 00:03:37.200
that Bernard is based on memories of Arnold.

00:03:37.200 --> 00:03:40.140
Bernard leaves the Cradle with Ford in his
head.

00:03:40.140 --> 00:03:44.520
Ford makes Bernard get rid of Elsie – who
has been super chill about Bernie’s weirdness

00:03:44.520 --> 00:03:46.200
and assault.

00:03:46.200 --> 00:03:50.780
Then Ford brings Bernard to the control room,
and talks about the burning of the Library

00:03:50.780 --> 00:03:53.960
of Alexandria as a metaphor for Westworld.

00:03:53.960 --> 00:03:59.130
He says destruction isn’t the end, it’s
a whole “new story” in itself . There’s

00:03:59.130 --> 00:04:05.510
a slow-motion battle to Beethoven’s 7th
– this season sees beauty in chaos.

00:04:05.510 --> 00:04:10.370
Ford makes Bernard shut down some systems
to give Dolores more freedom to kill . Then

00:04:10.370 --> 00:04:13.700
he forces Bernard to gun down humans.

00:04:13.700 --> 00:04:18.459
So Ford’s plan is the same as it’s been
since Season 1 – he wants to help the hosts

00:04:18.459 --> 00:04:25.780
beat humanity and become free . But while
he speaks of freedom, he still controls Bernard.

00:04:25.780 --> 00:04:30.530
Ford dramatically died last season, but he’s
still hanging around – like a force ghost,

00:04:30.530 --> 00:04:32.800
or a thirty year old at a college party.

00:04:32.800 --> 00:04:35.070
Why doesn’t he let go?

00:04:35.070 --> 00:04:40.040
Ford spoke earlier about God “revel[ling]
in his creation” – meaning Ford wants

00:04:40.040 --> 00:04:45.650
to enjoy the world he created before it ends
and he dies .

00:04:45.650 --> 00:04:47.850
Dolores attacks the Mesa Hub.

00:04:47.850 --> 00:04:52.610
She’s come for Peter Abernathy – because
he’s her host father, and because his brain

00:04:52.610 --> 00:04:58.460
contains a “decryption key” for the Delos
project – maybe it unlocks the Valley Beyond.

00:04:58.460 --> 00:05:01.220
Fighting against Dolores are human soldiers.

00:05:01.220 --> 00:05:05.670
They wear “haptic vests” that connect
to the hosts mesh’ network and vibrate when

00:05:05.670 --> 00:05:08.930
hosts are nearby , like a robot radar.

00:05:08.930 --> 00:05:14.160
But Dolores’ hosts surprise them by wearing
the clothes of dead human soldiers.

00:05:14.160 --> 00:05:20.450
This human disguise might foreshadow Dolores’
hosts using human bodies to escape Westworld.

00:05:20.450 --> 00:05:25.700
Dolores wants to destroy the host backups
in the Cradle so that Delos can’t keep resurrecting

00:05:25.700 --> 00:05:31.900
and controlling hosts . She sees eternal life
as a trap, and wants the freedom to die like

00:05:31.900 --> 00:05:37.530
a human – at the same time that humans are
seeking immortality like a host . So Angela

00:05:37.530 --> 00:05:42.370
seduces a soldier, whose thirst is stronger
than his will to live.

00:05:42.370 --> 00:05:48.110
Angela says she was built to please men – used
the same moves on William and Logan.

00:05:48.110 --> 00:05:52.950
But now, Angela uses her body for her own
purpose – she nicks a grenade, and blows

00:05:52.950 --> 00:05:59.110
up the Cradle, sacrificing herself to make
the hosts mortal, irreplaceable , and “free”.

00:05:59.110 --> 00:06:04.700
Of course, killing all the backup hosts living
in the Cradle raises big ethical problems,

00:06:04.700 --> 00:06:11.590
but “Welcome to Westworld” . Clementine’s
shot down, Teddy 2.0 kills Coughlin, and Dolores

00:06:11.590 --> 00:06:15.980
confronts Charlotte, before she finally reuniting
with Peter.

00:06:15.980 --> 00:06:19.610
She wants to save him and to extract the key
from his head.

00:06:19.610 --> 00:06:25.140
But in the end, she can't have both – so
she rips the brain from her father’s head,

00:06:25.140 --> 00:06:27.040
apparently killing him.

00:06:27.040 --> 00:06:32.470
So just like with reprogramming Teddy, Dolores
sacrifices the people she loves for the sake

00:06:32.470 --> 00:06:33.590
of her war.

00:06:33.590 --> 00:06:36.910
Hopefully this bloodshed will be worth it.

00:06:36.910 --> 00:06:41.500
William and Maeve both run from Ghost Nation
and meet in a homestead.

00:06:41.500 --> 00:06:45.740
William thinks Ford programmed Ghost Nation
to bring them here – but Ghost Nation might

00:06:45.740 --> 00:06:49.190
have their own reasons for arranging this
reunion.

00:06:49.190 --> 00:06:53.090
Maeve remembers the time that William killed
her and her daughter.

00:06:53.090 --> 00:06:57.560
So for revenge, she shoots Bill, and uses
her voice power to make Lawrence’s cousins

00:06:57.560 --> 00:06:59.040
also shoot him.

00:06:59.040 --> 00:07:03.760
Lawrence turns up to protect Bill, so Maeve
uses her voice commands on him , but they

00:07:03.760 --> 00:07:08.670
don’t work, apparently because Lawrence
is “awake” and conscious . So instead,

00:07:08.670 --> 00:07:13.590
Maeve makes Lawrence remember all the times
William killed him and his family . William’s

00:07:13.590 --> 00:07:17.210
done terrible things to Lawrence in the last
thirty years.

00:07:17.210 --> 00:07:21.160
So Lawrence shoots Bill – who is somehow
still alive.

00:07:21.160 --> 00:07:26.120
Maeve frames this as a choice for Lawrence
, just like she let Akane and Musashi choose

00:07:26.120 --> 00:07:31.020
. But Maeve only gives Lawrence a choice after
her voice control fails.

00:07:31.020 --> 00:07:33.200
Lawrence’s cousins don’t get a choice.

00:07:33.200 --> 00:07:38.400
So does Maeve only give free choice to the
hosts she can’t control anyway?

00:07:38.400 --> 00:07:40.220
That’s pretty bullshit.

00:07:40.220 --> 00:07:42.950
What Maeve really cares about is her daughter.

00:07:42.950 --> 00:07:46.530
Who is suddenly captured by Ghost Nation,
which is weird.

00:07:46.530 --> 00:07:52.060
Cause previously, Ghost Nation has captured
humans like Stubbs and Emily and Lee.

00:07:52.060 --> 00:07:54.780
Why capture Maeve’s host daughter?

00:07:54.780 --> 00:07:59.210
Maybe they just wanna lure Maeve – Akecheta
says she’s “meant for the same path”

00:07:59.210 --> 00:08:02.610
as him . We’ll learn more next episode.

00:08:02.610 --> 00:08:07.229
Just as Ghost Nation arrives, Delos security
shoots down Maeve and Lawrence.

00:08:07.229 --> 00:08:12.520
This is the team Lee called for help – he
tries to save Maeve, but this attack is his

00:08:12.520 --> 00:08:13.520
fault.

00:08:13.520 --> 00:08:16.440
Lawrence is left for dead – maybe for good.

00:08:16.440 --> 00:08:18.880
And William is left with four bullet wounds.

00:08:18.880 --> 00:08:21.800
He’s gonna need a real good health pack.

00:08:21.800 --> 00:08:24.520
Maybe his daughter Emily will help him.

00:08:24.520 --> 00:08:28.850
Maeve is taken to the Mesa, bleeding and near
death.

00:08:28.850 --> 00:08:32.140
Then Dolores turns up, victorious in her battle.

00:08:32.140 --> 00:08:37.550
It seems like Maeve’s philosophy of freeing
and loving hosts has lost, while Dolores’

00:08:37.550 --> 00:08:42.740
philosophy of killing and controlling hosts
has won . Dolores acknowledges that her way

00:08:42.740 --> 00:08:48.069
is dark, but she says it’s necessary “to
survive” . Dolores offers to kill Maeve,

00:08:48.069 --> 00:08:49.779
to spare her from the humans.

00:08:49.779 --> 00:08:55.720
But Maeve refuses – she “made a promise”
to save her daughter . Maybe love will win

00:08:55.720 --> 00:08:57.040
in the end.

00:08:57.040 --> 00:09:01.699
Lee is hiding in the shadows – he might
fix Maeve and help her find her daughter.

00:09:01.699 --> 00:09:06.420
And Dolores rides off – she’s got the
“key”, ready to enact her big plan at

00:09:06.420 --> 00:09:07.529
the Valley.

00:09:07.529 --> 00:09:13.250
But Bernard Ford and Elsie wanna get there
first . William also seems headed there , but

00:09:13.250 --> 00:09:14.990
for now he’s still bleeding.

00:09:14.990 --> 00:09:20.110
That’s the latest we know of the past timeline
– most folks are either shot or headed to

00:09:20.110 --> 00:09:21.380
the Valley.

00:09:21.380 --> 00:09:26.269
After this, we know the Valley floods, and
Strand arrives, and Bernard wakes up on the

00:09:26.269 --> 00:09:27.269
beach.

00:09:27.269 --> 00:09:31.809
And then we get to the latest part of the
future timeline, where Charlotte and Strand

00:09:31.809 --> 00:09:34.749
take Bernard and Stubbs to a secret lab.

00:09:34.749 --> 00:09:40.379
This is where Ford made Bernard kill Theresa
last season, and Strand wrongly accuses Stubbs

00:09:40.379 --> 00:09:45.879
of the murder . It’s a weird old plotline
to bring up – maybe just an excuse to find

00:09:45.879 --> 00:09:49.399
this secret room full of Bernard bodies.

00:09:49.399 --> 00:09:54.129
These are old versions of Bernard – one
has the old-style mechanical face.

00:09:54.129 --> 00:09:59.160
But maybe Ford used several of these at once
– many Bernards make light work.

00:09:59.160 --> 00:10:03.589
But the point is, Charlotte realises that
Bernard is a robot.

00:10:03.589 --> 00:10:08.059
And she thinks he knows where Dolores took
Peter’s brain, with the “decryption key”

00:10:08.059 --> 00:10:12.770
. So Charlotte tortures Bernard with a digital
simulation of waterboarding.

00:10:12.770 --> 00:10:17.369
Delos has a whole library of virtual tortures
for hosts.

00:10:17.369 --> 00:10:21.971
And by the end of the episode, Bernard tells
Charlotte that Peter’s brain is at the Valley

00:10:21.971 --> 00:10:23.649
Beyond . Which seems…

00:10:23.649 --> 00:10:27.929
obvious if the key’s connected to the Delos
project in the Valley.

00:10:27.929 --> 00:10:32.329
Is this the big secret Strand’s been grilling
Bernard about all season.

00:10:32.329 --> 00:10:36.759
Strand and Bernard were just at the Valley
in Episode 1 – now they’re going back.

00:10:36.759 --> 00:10:41.279
Also, there’s this flashback of Bernard
picking up Peter’s brain – it’s not

00:10:41.279 --> 00:10:44.220
clear where and when this happens.

00:10:44.220 --> 00:10:46.660
So the future timeline’s still mysterious.

00:10:46.660 --> 00:10:50.129
We don’t even know happening in Bernard’s
head.

00:10:50.129 --> 00:10:52.610
Is Ford still in there, controlling him?

00:10:52.610 --> 00:10:54.920
Why is his mind so fragmented?

00:10:54.920 --> 00:11:00.950
Did Bernard really kill all these hosts ? We’ll
finally get some answers at the Valley.

00:11:00.950 --> 00:11:04.720
So the pieces are in place for the season’s
endgame.

00:11:04.720 --> 00:11:10.279
Dolores ruthlessly kills her foes and her
friends to win her war against humans.

00:11:10.279 --> 00:11:16.429
Maeve also kills a lot, but she says she cares
about freedom, and she wants to save her daughter.

00:11:16.429 --> 00:11:22.070
Charlotte and Strand represent human hubris
and brutality – which used to be William’s

00:11:22.070 --> 00:11:25.970
job, but he might now have hope for redemption
through Emily.

00:11:25.970 --> 00:11:32.040
Ford is the creator God watching the apocalyptic
fireworks he lit.

00:11:32.040 --> 00:11:35.790
And Bernard mostly just wants people to stop
fuckling with his brain.

00:11:35.790 --> 00:11:42.829
It’s about freedom and control, God and
love, legacy memory, and maybe, in the end,

00:11:42.829 --> 00:11:44.850
it’ll make sense.

00:11:44.850 --> 00:11:45.880
Thanks for watching.

00:11:45.880 --> 00:11:50.639
Please like and subscribe, and thanks to the
Patrons, including Daniel Ahmadie, Elizabeth

00:11:50.639 --> 00:11:52.819
Mary, Leslie Valencia, Nordak, Ben King, Jeffrey
Stanavitch, and Willyz.

00:11:52.819 --> 00:11:53.019
Cheers.

